1
00:00:10,211 --> 00:00:12,129
Previously on.

2
00:00:17,385 --> 00:00:18,177
Why?

3
00:00:18,720 --> 00:00:19,929
The reception is this weekend.

4
00:00:20,221 --> 00:00:23,141
The left sleeve of the jacket is slightly shorter than the right.

5
00:00:23,683 --> 00:00:24,225
Damn it!

6
00:00:24,684 --> 00:00:26,352
My friend needs waiters.

7
00:00:26,603 --> 00:00:27,395
In what area?

8
00:00:27,645 --> 00:00:29,189
In Leon Prater's mansion.

9
00:00:29,564 --> 00:00:31,483
He's hitting on my son, asshole.

10
00:00:31,733 --> 00:00:33,401
Of course, room service.

11
00:00:34,277 --> 00:00:35,528
Charlie came to see me at work.

12
00:00:35,779 --> 00:00:36,780
She's hitting on your son.

13
00:00:37,280 --> 00:00:39,783
It's time for me to pay Charlie a surprise visit.

14
00:00:40,784 --> 00:00:42,285
She's taking care of her mother.

15
00:00:42,744 --> 00:00:44,079
You killed my mom.

16
00:00:44,454 --> 00:00:45,163
I'm not like that.

17
00:00:45,705 --> 00:00:47,124
Leave my son alone.

18
00:00:50,836 --> 00:00:53,422
I need to speak with Mr. Leon Prater.

19
00:00:53,964 --> 00:00:55,716
How do you know this guy?

20
00:00:56,341 --> 00:00:57,259
You mean Mr. Schmidt?

21
00:00:57,551 --> 00:00:58,677
No, this is Dexter Morgan.

22
00:00:59,636 --> 00:01:02,180
We worked together in the Miami homicide division.

23
00:01:03,348 --> 00:01:06,060
Given the circumstances, let's have the meeting in the vault.

24
00:01:06,602 --> 00:01:07,561
Dexter Morgan.

25
00:01:08,604 --> 00:01:11,065
Control yourself. No foolishness.

26
00:01:11,607 --> 00:01:13,275
I know exactly who you are.

27
00:01:14,318 --> 00:01:15,319
And I like it.

28
00:01:17,279 --> 00:01:20,533
I have extensive dossiers on serial killers from all over the world.

29
00:01:21,659 --> 00:01:22,618
What will happen to Angel?

30
00:01:23,327 --> 00:01:25,746
This is the price of your admission.

31
00:01:27,998 --> 00:01:29,542
Goodbye, collaboration.

32
00:01:41,262 --> 00:01:42,221
Dexter Morgan.

33
00:01:42,763 --> 00:01:43,472
F**k you.

34
00:01:52,688 --> 00:01:53,773
That was incredible.

35
00:01:54,482 --> 00:01:57,527
You meant to say stupid. Damn stupid.

36
00:01:58,069 --> 00:01:58,819
I killed him.

37
00:01:59,320 --> 00:02:00,321
You killed a cop.

38
00:02:01,489 --> 00:02:06,077
I've put up with these psychos for years and easily got rid of them for you.

39
00:02:06,536 --> 00:02:08,538
But I didn't sign up for this.

40
00:02:09,330 --> 00:02:11,124
Yeah, I know, it got out of control.

41
00:02:11,624 --> 00:02:13,668
Aren't you listening? You killed a cop.

42
00:02:14,919 --> 00:02:18,256
Before all the cops in the city arrive at your reception.

43
00:02:18,506 --> 00:02:19,799
I'll deal with them.

44
00:02:20,425 --> 00:02:22,886
Just like everything in there, it will resolve itself.

45
00:02:23,678 --> 00:02:25,430
You're just going to leave him there?

46
00:02:25,722 --> 00:02:26,598
What other choice is there?

47
00:02:26,848 --> 00:02:27,641
Let him go?

48
00:02:28,099 --> 00:02:30,602
Introduce him to the police commissioner and ask him to dance?

49
00:02:31,311 --> 00:02:33,313
Alright, I get it.

50
00:02:33,855 --> 00:02:34,439
Yeah.

51
00:02:36,191 --> 00:02:37,609
Remember the rule of threes.

52
00:02:38,527 --> 00:02:42,531
3 minutes without oxygen, 3 days without water, 3 weeks without food.

53
00:02:44,324 --> 00:02:45,534
There's enough oxygen.

54
00:02:47,494 --> 00:02:48,453
So, 3 days.

55
00:02:50,497 --> 00:02:53,166
He'll either make it or die in there.

56
00:02:58,422 --> 00:02:59,631
I'm needed downstairs.

57
00:03:01,300 --> 00:03:03,135
Wait here and guard the vault.

58
00:03:04,303 --> 00:03:06,138
There's a first aid kit in the dresser, treat your wound.

59
00:03:06,388 --> 00:03:07,431
I need you in top shape.

60
00:03:11,477 --> 00:03:12,144
Damn it.

61
00:03:18,108 --> 00:03:20,903
Angel was killed with this gun, I need to wipe the prints.

62
00:03:24,240 --> 00:03:25,574
There has to be another way out.

63
00:03:35,167 --> 00:03:36,585
I definitely wasn't planning on dying.

64
00:03:41,841 --> 00:03:43,467
But neither was Batista.

65
00:03:58,064 --> 00:03:59,982
Rest in peace, Angel.

66
00:04:01,108 --> 00:04:02,777
You were a good cop.

67
00:04:04,654 --> 00:04:06,239
And a good person.

68
00:04:11,828 --> 00:04:13,705
Oops, you did it again.

69
00:04:16,291 --> 00:04:18,501
That's what happens when you pretend to be someone else.

70
00:04:19,544 --> 00:04:21,129
I told Angel to go home.

71
00:04:21,504 --> 00:04:22,881
Batista couldn't leave.

72
00:04:23,631 --> 00:04:26,384
He considered you his best friend for 20 years.

73
00:04:27,218 --> 00:04:31,640
And mourned your death for 10 years, only to find out you're a crazy killer.

74
00:04:32,349 --> 00:04:33,725
And you didn't give a damn about him.

75
00:04:36,144 --> 00:04:38,980
Then why does his death hurt my heart so much?

76
00:04:39,481 --> 00:04:44,570
You're still listening to your fake father instead of your blood brother.

77
00:04:45,320 --> 00:04:48,824
I offered you a life with someone who understands you.

78
00:04:50,075 --> 00:04:50,868
And you killed me.

79
00:04:51,702 --> 00:04:54,538
Then you had a second chance with Prater's club.

80
00:04:55,247 --> 00:04:57,583
And you screwed that up too. For what?

81
00:04:58,167 --> 00:05:04,798
For people like Batista, your so-called friend, who said "F**k you" before he died.

82
00:05:10,221 --> 00:05:12,681
I'm glad I killed you when I had the chance.

83
00:05:13,599 --> 00:05:15,017
Dexter. Resurrection.

84
00:05:31,909 --> 00:05:33,661
And justice for all.

85
00:05:35,246 --> 00:05:36,330
Three days, huh?

86
00:05:43,212 --> 00:05:47,758
If I locked the Bay Harbor Butcher in a room with a gun, I'd never open the door.

87
00:05:51,262 --> 00:06:02,732
And if you don't want to start slicing Batista into sashimi, you'll die here, and your dried-up, emaciated corpse will become Prater's best trophy.

88
00:06:03,858 --> 00:06:05,318
I'm not going to die here!

89
00:06:17,455 --> 00:06:18,456
Quinn.

90
00:06:20,541 --> 00:06:21,125
Damn.

91
00:06:21,584 --> 00:06:22,126
Shit.

92
00:06:22,668 --> 00:06:24,420
I'll have to unlock his phone.

93
00:06:25,379 --> 00:06:26,381
Sorry, bro.

94
00:06:33,429 --> 00:06:34,389
Hey, Angel.

95
00:06:34,931 --> 00:06:36,558
A detective from New York called me.

96
00:06:37,225 --> 00:06:38,268
What the hell are you doing there?

97
00:06:38,685 --> 00:06:40,562
Go home, I'm worried about you.

98
00:06:41,271 --> 00:06:43,773
And listen, I'm calling you because I can't stand your replacement.

99
00:06:44,441 --> 00:06:45,442
He pisses me off.

100
00:06:46,568 --> 00:06:47,903
I miss him.

101
00:06:49,362 --> 00:06:50,906
But there's one person I can call.

102
00:06:53,491 --> 00:06:55,202
You came here to protect your son.

103
00:06:56,036 --> 00:06:57,537
You want to drag him into the lion's den?

104
00:06:58,288 --> 00:07:01,500
I promised to protect Harrison, if I die here, I won't be able to.

105
00:07:02,292 --> 00:07:05,587
You want to be a good father, not afraid of death.

106
00:07:07,756 --> 00:07:08,840
Maybe both.

107
00:07:16,348 --> 00:07:17,474
Damn, I'll answer.

108
00:07:18,433 --> 00:07:19,267
Batista.

109
00:07:24,231 --> 00:07:25,440
Who is Batista?

110
00:07:26,275 --> 00:07:28,527
A guy who won't leave me alone, as you can see.

111
00:07:32,114 --> 00:07:36,577
Hey, idiot. Harrison can't talk, his mouth is busy with me.

112
00:07:40,247 --> 00:07:41,248
Oh, okay.

113
00:07:43,459 --> 00:07:45,461
Your father wants to talk.

114
00:07:55,721 --> 00:07:57,014
Hey, dad. What happened?

115
00:07:57,723 --> 00:07:59,141
I'm sorry, but I need your help.

116
00:07:59,683 --> 00:08:01,310
Why are you calling from Batista's phone?

117
00:08:01,810 --> 00:08:02,770
Prater knows who I am.

118
00:08:02,811 --> 00:08:03,646
Dad, stop it.

119
00:08:04,522 --> 00:08:06,482
Why are you calling from Batista's phone?

120
00:08:07,525 --> 00:08:10,027
The last time you called from a cop's phone...

121
00:08:10,236 --> 00:08:12,655
Yes, Logan. I know. Harrison, listen to me.

122
00:08:14,448 --> 00:08:17,702
Prater killed Batista, and I'm next.

123
00:08:18,327 --> 00:08:19,078
Shit.

124
00:08:20,538 --> 00:08:21,706
What can I do?

125
00:08:24,584 --> 00:08:25,168
Damn it.

126
00:08:25,710 --> 00:08:27,253
Hey Harrison, how's it going?

127
00:08:27,754 --> 00:08:30,131
Is your offer still on the table?

128
00:08:30,715 --> 00:08:32,258
Oh, so you decided to work after all.

129
00:08:32,759 --> 00:08:34,427
Yeah, I was just picking up groceries.

130
00:08:34,677 --> 00:08:35,720
I'll send you the address.

131
00:08:36,262 --> 00:08:36,971
Great.

132
00:09:15,487 --> 00:09:16,363
What is this?

133
00:09:21,201 --> 00:09:23,120
Prater's file on all serial killers.

134
00:09:23,537 --> 00:09:25,539
Maybe the code for the vault is here too.

135
00:09:26,582 --> 00:09:27,416
Somewhere.

136
00:09:33,464 --> 00:09:34,423
Morris Cooper.

137
00:09:40,220 --> 00:09:43,432
You think Prater left a sticker that says "Vault Code"?

138
00:09:45,559 --> 00:09:46,477
I'll crack it.

139
00:09:47,144 --> 00:09:48,646
It's an eight-digit number.

140
00:09:49,146 --> 00:09:50,147
You have one attempt.

141
00:09:50,731 --> 00:09:55,277
If someone enters the wrong code just once...

142
00:10:01,242 --> 00:10:02,368
Charlotte Brown.

143
00:10:03,160 --> 00:10:04,119
Wait, Charlotte.

144
00:10:05,287 --> 00:10:06,205
Charlie Brown.

145
00:10:06,622 --> 00:10:08,249
That's why she's so grumpy.

146
00:10:11,210 --> 00:10:13,421
Prater likes to keep an eye on his employees.

147
00:10:21,596 --> 00:10:23,264
Prater likes to keep an eye on everyone.

148
00:10:24,223 --> 00:10:26,517
What if you're remembered as the Dark Passenger?

149
00:10:26,767 --> 00:10:27,351
Yes.

150
00:10:28,477 --> 00:10:30,229
We need to destroy all the files.

151
00:10:30,605 --> 00:10:31,439
If we get out...

152
00:10:31,689 --> 00:10:33,482
He definitely wrote it down somewhere.

153
00:10:35,401 --> 00:10:36,444
Cooper Morris.

154
00:10:40,156 --> 00:10:42,325
Prater talked about him. He killed his parents.

155
00:10:43,284 --> 00:10:44,118
And others.

156
00:10:47,121 --> 00:10:50,708
Or Prater didn't write down the code because he never forgets it.

157
00:10:53,252 --> 00:10:54,128
Today's date.

158
00:10:54,420 --> 00:10:56,672
Prater is holding a reception on the anniversary of his parents' death.

159
00:10:57,423 --> 00:11:02,095
When Cooper Morris killed Prater's parents, his life changed that night.

160
00:11:02,678 --> 00:11:04,305
An important date for the code, right?

161
00:11:04,764 --> 00:11:07,183
If the alarm goes off, the cops will rush in.

162
00:11:07,517 --> 00:11:08,184
Are you sure?

163
00:11:08,476 --> 00:11:08,977
I'm sure.

164
00:11:09,602 --> 00:11:10,562
On your life.

165
00:11:11,187 --> 00:11:12,313
And Harrison's life?

166
00:11:15,817 --> 00:11:20,530
Attention, waiters! Behind these curtains are the most influential bigwigs in New York.

167
00:11:21,031 --> 00:11:24,242
Wine glasses should always be full, clear plates immediately.

168
00:11:24,617 --> 00:11:26,202
Always be ready.

169
00:11:26,453 --> 00:11:27,245
Do you understand me?

170
00:11:27,537 --> 00:11:28,080
Yes.

171
00:11:28,330 --> 00:11:31,249
Be attentive, observant, and don't be silent.

172
00:11:31,666 --> 00:11:32,250
Okay.

173
00:11:32,667 --> 00:11:33,126
Okay.

174
00:11:36,463 --> 00:11:37,297
I'm inside.

175
00:11:37,672 --> 00:11:38,423
Excellent.

176
00:11:39,424 --> 00:11:40,842
I need a better view.

177
00:11:41,218 --> 00:11:44,221
Guys, let's go. What are we waiting for? Get to work, quickly.

178
00:11:44,554 --> 00:11:45,847
Yes, we need to work.

179
00:11:46,556 --> 00:11:47,307
Okay.

180
00:11:55,649 --> 00:11:56,316
Where do I go?

181
00:11:56,858 --> 00:11:59,486
The penthouse in the east wing of the mansion.

182
00:12:00,529 --> 00:12:01,238
Got it.

183
00:12:13,917 --> 00:12:14,751
Claudette.

184
00:12:15,627 --> 00:12:17,462
Wow, you look so...

185
00:12:19,089 --> 00:12:20,674
That color really suits you.

186
00:12:21,299 --> 00:12:22,801
The sleeves are different lengths.

187
00:12:27,431 --> 00:12:28,348
Where do I go now?

188
00:12:28,890 --> 00:12:31,435
All I see is champagne.

189
00:12:32,602 --> 00:12:33,311
Damn it.

190
00:12:38,275 --> 00:12:39,526
Should I go up the stairs?

191
00:12:40,235 --> 00:12:42,529
No, you can't get to the penthouse that way.

192
00:12:43,655 --> 00:12:45,073
Over there, what's that door?

193
00:12:45,866 --> 00:12:47,034
The service kitchen.

194
00:12:47,326 --> 00:12:48,035
Go there.

195
00:12:48,327 --> 00:12:50,037
Keep an eye on Prater and Charlie.

196
00:12:50,287 --> 00:12:52,247
If they see you, they'll know something's wrong.

197
00:12:52,706 --> 00:12:55,542
I work with rich people all the time, they never notice the help.

198
00:12:55,793 --> 00:12:56,877
Excuse me.

199
00:12:57,294 --> 00:12:58,420
Really, really.

200
00:12:58,796 --> 00:13:02,174
Leon, I saw a charter for your yacht is being auctioned off at the silent auction.

201
00:13:02,758 --> 00:13:05,344
We just brought it in from St. Barts, Mr. Mayor.

202
00:13:05,719 --> 00:13:07,721
Chelsea Piers, right? How do you like it there?

203
00:13:08,222 --> 00:13:10,933
I can tell you a lot about Chelsea Piers. I think so too.

204
00:13:11,392 --> 00:13:11,976
Damn.

205
00:13:12,852 --> 00:13:14,478
I think that's it.

206
00:13:15,021 --> 00:13:16,022
Don't confess.

207
00:13:29,201 --> 00:13:31,662
Past that fridge on the left. Is that a staircase?

208
00:13:38,461 --> 00:13:39,462
Son of a bitch.

209
00:13:39,921 --> 00:13:41,130
Harrison, get out.

210
00:13:41,631 --> 00:13:42,882
Where do you think you're going?

211
00:13:43,716 --> 00:13:45,801
I was actually looking for you.

212
00:13:47,011 --> 00:13:48,638
One of your waiters is really high.

213
00:13:49,180 --> 00:13:51,265
He might become a problem out there on the front line.

214
00:13:51,682 --> 00:13:52,683
Can you show me?

215
00:13:53,851 --> 00:13:56,354
He's right over there.

216
00:13:57,146 --> 00:13:58,481
Thanks for the warning.

217
00:14:00,108 --> 00:14:01,484
Good move, son.

218
00:14:02,235 --> 00:14:04,404
Yeah, remind me to make it up to Lance.

219
00:14:10,618 --> 00:14:12,120
Look at all of you!

220
00:14:12,412 --> 00:14:15,039
Welcome everyone to my favorite night of the year.

221
00:14:15,373 --> 00:14:20,336
The 10th annual gala honoring the best of New York.

222
00:14:21,504 --> 00:14:23,173
The penthouse is five floors up.

223
00:14:23,798 --> 00:14:25,508
The stairs go up that high, yeah?

224
00:14:26,259 --> 00:14:26,718
Yeah.

225
00:14:28,011 --> 00:14:28,720
This is the fifth.

226
00:14:29,346 --> 00:14:30,472
And this is to the roof.

227
00:14:31,473 --> 00:14:32,641
I think I'm here.

228
00:14:39,814 --> 00:14:40,565
Locked.

229
00:14:41,691 --> 00:14:43,443
Do you have something to pick it with?

230
00:14:46,363 --> 00:14:49,699
Can you pick the lock like I showed you in Iron Lake?

231
00:14:53,495 --> 00:14:54,496
It's not working.

232
00:15:00,710 --> 00:15:02,045
Harrison Morgan.

233
00:15:02,629 --> 00:15:06,425
Too much trouble for a man you barely know.

234
00:15:19,271 --> 00:15:20,022
Sit down.

235
00:15:24,234 --> 00:15:26,528
Dad, what should I do? Give the phone to Charlie.

236
00:15:32,242 --> 00:15:34,328
My dad wants to talk to you.

237
00:15:35,537 --> 00:15:37,331
Ah, Charlie Brown. Good to see you.

238
00:15:37,581 --> 00:15:39,458
I need you to open the vault.

239
00:15:39,875 --> 00:15:44,463
As tempting as that sounds, I think I'll leave the Bay Harbor Butcher securely locked up.

240
00:15:45,339 --> 00:15:47,216
Yeah, that's about what I expected.

241
00:15:48,092 --> 00:15:48,717
What's that?

242
00:15:49,385 --> 00:15:52,430
A little something I found in your boss's secret file cabinet.

243
00:15:52,680 --> 00:15:56,058
Timestamped right before Mia's tragic suicide.

244
00:15:56,434 --> 00:15:57,643
There's a whole file on you.

245
00:15:58,102 --> 00:16:01,522
Documents, phone logs, surveillance photos.

246
00:16:02,064 --> 00:16:05,443
Looks like Prater has been documenting your dirty work for a long time.

247
00:16:07,403 --> 00:16:08,779
That bastard.

248
00:16:12,116 --> 00:16:14,785
The thing is, Charlie, there are a lot of cops downstairs.

249
00:16:15,578 --> 00:16:18,915
You'd be surprised how many of them have their AirDrop open to everyone.

250
00:16:19,415 --> 00:16:20,833
It'll only take me a second.

251
00:16:25,713 --> 00:16:29,217
And if you go to jail, who will take care of your mother?

252
00:16:32,261 --> 00:16:33,471
Here's the deal.

253
00:16:34,180 --> 00:16:37,934
I'll destroy everything, including the copies I made on Batista's phone.

254
00:16:39,268 --> 00:16:42,355
You just need to let Harrison go and open the vault.

255
00:16:43,106 --> 00:16:44,774
You won't see or hear from us again.

256
00:16:45,316 --> 00:16:47,109
You'll leave my mother alive.

257
00:16:47,485 --> 00:16:49,153
So, here's how it's going to be.

258
00:16:49,612 --> 00:16:53,450
I'll let your son go, and then I'll leave.

259
00:16:54,451 --> 00:16:56,411
And you'll die in there.

260
00:16:57,287 --> 00:17:03,168
Publish those files early, and well, you know how good I am at finding people.

261
00:17:03,418 --> 00:17:09,799
In a month, in a year, in two, I'll kill your son, after torturing him first.

262
00:17:10,634 --> 00:17:14,471
One look at my file and you'll understand what I'm capable of.

263
00:17:15,639 --> 00:17:22,812
And now, if you'll excuse me, I have unfinished business with my former employer.

264
00:17:27,526 --> 00:17:31,446
You should leave too.

265
00:17:34,199 --> 00:17:36,493
There's nothing good in there.

266
00:17:53,259 --> 00:17:54,427
Harrison, are you still on the line?

267
00:17:55,178 --> 00:17:56,012
Yeah, I'm here.

268
00:17:58,265 --> 00:17:59,391
The battery is dying.

269
00:18:00,100 --> 00:18:01,518
Switch to audio only.

270
00:18:03,186 --> 00:18:09,943
I'm pretty sure I have the code for the vault. The passage is through the wine room, there's a keypad on the wall by the door.

271
00:18:10,902 --> 00:18:12,487
But we only have one try.

272
00:18:13,071 --> 00:18:18,827
If I make a mistake, the alarm will go off. Then you need to get out of here before hundreds of cops rush up the stairs.

273
00:18:19,411 --> 00:18:20,328
No pressure.

274
00:18:21,204 --> 00:18:23,498
Harrison, you don't have to do this.

275
00:18:24,041 --> 00:18:25,959
You can leave right now, I'll understand.

276
00:18:33,425 --> 00:18:34,676
Just give me the code, dad.

277
00:18:38,222 --> 00:18:49,775
0-3-2-6-1-9-8... Wait, stop.

278
00:18:50,150 --> 00:18:50,734
What?

279
00:19:01,203 --> 00:19:03,664
That might not be the right code. Can you start over?

280
00:19:04,123 --> 00:19:08,794
Are you sure? You just said... Self-doubt doesn't exactly inspire confidence.

281
00:19:18,178 --> 00:19:19,638
Look at everything, start over.

282
00:19:22,099 --> 00:19:22,641
Ready?

283
00:19:23,350 --> 00:19:23,809
Yeah.

284
00:19:24,810 --> 00:19:32,318
8-2-6-6-1-9-3-4.

285
00:19:33,527 --> 00:19:34,862
Got it all down.

286
00:19:38,449 --> 00:19:39,074
Okay.

287
00:19:40,242 --> 00:19:40,910
Damn it.

288
00:19:42,745 --> 00:19:43,496
Dad?

289
00:19:46,248 --> 00:19:47,041
Dad?

290
00:19:47,625 --> 00:19:48,376
Shit.

291
00:19:52,421 --> 00:19:54,715
Dad, you want me to...

292
00:20:07,353 --> 00:20:08,354
Sports!

293
00:20:08,479 --> 00:20:10,022
Poker, casino!

294
00:20:10,147 --> 00:20:11,649
All of this can make you money.

295
00:20:12,108 --> 00:20:15,319
Find the 1xBet website, register in one click...

296
00:20:15,444 --> 00:20:17,822
...and get a super bonus of $400.

297
00:20:32,086 --> 00:20:33,129
You're doing great.

298
00:20:33,671 --> 00:20:35,464
What the hell is this place?

299
00:20:36,382 --> 00:20:39,761
Wait here, I'm going to grab a few things and don't let the door close.

300
00:20:50,188 --> 00:20:53,441
Son, you better quit while you're ahead.

301
00:20:53,691 --> 00:20:54,484
I want this.

302
00:20:55,026 --> 00:20:57,028
First, we need to deal with Prater.

303
00:20:57,487 --> 00:21:00,323
I'll deal with it, but right above a gala crawling with cops is not the time.

304
00:21:00,740 --> 00:21:02,367
I need to control everything.

305
00:21:08,289 --> 00:21:09,332
This is mine.

306
00:21:11,126 --> 00:21:12,460
Thanks for the bag, Sal.

307
00:21:15,630 --> 00:21:16,256
Let's go.

308
00:21:18,258 --> 00:21:19,634
Tell me we're getting out of here.

309
00:21:22,137 --> 00:21:23,013
What's wrong?

310
00:21:23,138 --> 00:21:23,722
Damn it.

311
00:21:24,222 --> 00:21:25,724
Dad, I forgot something in the vault.

312
00:21:26,016 --> 00:21:26,516
What exactly?

313
00:21:26,766 --> 00:21:28,476
The fake thumbprint.

314
00:21:29,060 --> 00:21:31,646
I'll add that to the list of things you'll explain to me later.

315
00:21:32,272 --> 00:21:35,358
This is my only way out, but you can escape the same way.

316
00:21:35,775 --> 00:21:37,360
Through the gala? Are you crazy?

317
00:21:37,611 --> 00:21:39,696
Like you said, nobody notices the help.

318
00:21:40,030 --> 00:21:41,239
No, I mean, I'm not leaving you.

319
00:21:41,865 --> 00:21:44,242
Right now, Charlie could be telling Prater you're upstairs.

320
00:21:44,451 --> 00:21:46,620
I won't let you wait around to see what he does.

321
00:21:48,038 --> 00:21:50,332
I need to know you're safe.

322
00:21:51,124 --> 00:21:51,875
I'll be fine.

323
00:21:56,129 --> 00:21:57,047
Harrison...

324
00:21:58,048 --> 00:22:02,761
If something happens, I want you to know, I'm really glad you didn't kill me.

325
00:22:03,428 --> 00:22:04,388
Me too.

326
00:22:12,938 --> 00:22:15,524
LP, hey. Great party.

327
00:22:16,066 --> 00:22:18,652
Yeah. Listen, when can I catch you for a photo with the officers?

328
00:22:19,069 --> 00:22:20,529
I'll put it on the schedule.

329
00:22:23,198 --> 00:22:25,534
Okay. Wait a second, I'll be right back.

330
00:22:27,870 --> 00:22:29,204
Let's go to my office.

331
00:22:29,580 --> 00:22:30,581
This will do.

332
00:22:31,165 --> 00:22:32,958
What's going on? You shouldn't have come down.

333
00:22:33,292 --> 00:22:37,963
You talk as if I still work for you, but I've quit. I'm not covering for you anymore.

334
00:22:52,353 --> 00:22:53,437
You're not going anywhere.

335
00:22:53,729 --> 00:22:54,355
Why?

336
00:22:54,772 --> 00:22:57,191
Because you have a file with compromising photos of me?

337
00:22:57,566 --> 00:23:02,071
Wasn't it enough for you to hold my mother's health hostage? You had to own me.

338
00:23:02,446 --> 00:23:03,698
How do you know about the file?

339
00:23:05,408 --> 00:23:06,784
Where's that damn print?

340
00:23:25,511 --> 00:23:26,554
I'll disappear.

341
00:23:27,096 --> 00:23:33,728
You'll continue to pay for my mother's treatment, and all our secrets will remain secrets.

342
00:23:35,479 --> 00:23:39,400
Or... we'll do scorched earth.

343
00:23:40,234 --> 00:23:41,277
It's your call.

344
00:23:47,325 --> 00:23:48,451
Goodbye, Leon.

345
00:23:56,334 --> 00:23:59,337
Well then, let's take this evening to the next level.

346
00:24:04,342 --> 00:24:06,094
Is everyone having a good time?

347
00:24:06,511 --> 00:24:07,387
Yes!

348
00:24:10,098 --> 00:24:11,599
You okay? Alright.

349
00:24:12,684 --> 00:24:15,645
Looks like it's time for someone to open a couple more bottles.

350
00:24:20,275 --> 00:24:25,029
But let's not forget, this gala isn't about champagne and caviar.

351
00:24:25,738 --> 00:24:27,657
It's about fundraising.

352
00:25:00,315 --> 00:25:04,277
To help brave officers injured in the line of duty.

353
00:25:04,819 --> 00:25:10,366
That's why tonight, I will double every donation made before 9 p.m.

354
00:25:11,534 --> 00:25:14,454
Starting with my first contribution of a million dollars.

355
00:25:15,663 --> 00:25:17,665
So that's already 2 million.

356
00:25:21,461 --> 00:25:22,337
Yes!

357
00:25:28,426 --> 00:25:35,433
I don't want to hog the spotlight all evening, so let's welcome my co-conspirator in tonight's shenanigans.

358
00:25:36,434 --> 00:25:40,564
The NYPD Commissioner, Franklin McNamara.

359
00:25:42,399 --> 00:25:43,483
Come here.

360
00:25:45,443 --> 00:25:46,444
Great. Yeah.

361
00:25:46,695 --> 00:25:47,696
Well, yeah.

362
00:25:48,655 --> 00:25:54,202
So, well, I couldn't possibly...

363
00:26:00,375 --> 00:26:05,422
Mr. Prater, show me all the cameras at the north exit of the ballroom, inside and out.

364
00:26:10,760 --> 00:26:12,179
Turn off all the cameras.

365
00:26:12,429 --> 00:26:14,639
Sir, are you sure you want...? Do it.

366
00:26:16,224 --> 00:26:17,267
Give me your weapon.

367
00:26:17,767 --> 00:26:19,436
Give me your weapon.

368
00:26:38,413 --> 00:26:40,624
Hello, Harrison Morgan.

369
00:26:42,751 --> 00:26:46,922
Please, go down the stairs now. Thank you.

370
00:27:03,438 --> 00:27:05,440
Prater has plenty of expensive toys.

371
00:27:06,149 --> 00:27:07,776
But I will never be one of them.

372
00:27:12,406 --> 00:27:13,907
I'm almost out. Where are you?

373
00:27:14,241 --> 00:27:16,034
Why don't you come back up?

374
00:27:17,202 --> 00:27:19,788
Believe me, you don't want to miss this party.

375
00:27:20,330 --> 00:27:21,540
Where is my son?

376
00:27:23,375 --> 00:27:24,293
He's alive.

377
00:27:25,127 --> 00:27:26,086
Answer me!

378
00:27:26,628 --> 00:27:28,380
Where is my son?

379
00:27:31,717 --> 00:27:33,427
Tell your father where you are.

380
00:27:34,428 --> 00:27:36,472
We're in the wine room. Harrison!

381
00:27:37,431 --> 00:27:38,474
Bye, dad.

382
00:27:54,198 --> 00:27:56,367
It would be so much easier if I didn't care.

383
00:28:00,162 --> 00:28:02,081
Is this really the price of love?

384
00:28:05,042 --> 00:28:06,460
Kill that bastard!

385
00:28:18,597 --> 00:28:21,225
I'm glad you joined us.

386
00:28:22,518 --> 00:28:25,187
Each of us has dirt on the other.

387
00:28:26,063 --> 00:28:28,524
Let my son go, and you'll never see me again.

388
00:28:29,275 --> 00:28:32,820
None of this is necessary. Actually, it is.

389
00:28:34,113 --> 00:28:36,407
I've always admired people like you.

390
00:28:37,283 --> 00:28:42,371
But today I finally felt what it's like to be you, and it was amazing.

391
00:28:44,540 --> 00:28:54,342
So thank you for giving me, as you said, the itch, the need, the strong urge, the impulse.

392
00:28:55,093 --> 00:28:57,470
The impulse. Yes. The impulse. That's right.

393
00:28:58,012 --> 00:28:58,805
That's right.

394
00:28:59,389 --> 00:29:01,433
I finally experienced it.

395
00:29:02,684 --> 00:29:06,271
The mere thought of it makes my heart pound in my chest.

396
00:29:07,022 --> 00:29:09,399
Perhaps this was always my destiny.

397
00:29:10,317 --> 00:29:13,445
But if you hadn't pushed me, I would have never known.

398
00:29:15,197 --> 00:29:24,289
That's why I'm so proud that you will witness my first real, non-impulsive murder.

399
00:29:26,750 --> 00:29:28,293
Love has a price.

400
00:29:30,587 --> 00:29:32,214
And this is the ultimate price.

401
00:29:32,631 --> 00:29:35,467
If this is your big show, there's a better option.

402
00:29:36,134 --> 00:29:37,427
You can do better.

403
00:29:41,431 --> 00:29:42,516
Kill me.

404
00:29:44,226 --> 00:29:46,478
And you will become the greatest predator.

405
00:29:47,437 --> 00:29:49,356
The best of the best.

406
00:29:49,773 --> 00:29:52,442
The one who defeated the Bay Harbor Butcher.

407
00:29:53,402 --> 00:29:59,950
Kill me and make Harrison live with the consequences, just like the man who killed your parents did to you.

408
00:30:10,043 --> 00:30:12,629
Yes, but I can't leave a witness like Cooper Morris.

409
00:30:18,552 --> 00:30:20,554
I'm sorry I couldn't protect you.

410
00:30:21,597 --> 00:30:24,475
If you stay the night, you'll need protection.

411
00:30:37,738 --> 00:30:40,240
He won't ask anyone else to shoot you.

412
00:30:42,117 --> 00:30:43,452
What are we going to do?

413
00:30:44,078 --> 00:30:46,622
There is no "we". You're leaving, right now.

414
00:30:48,290 --> 00:30:49,833
Claudette is still in the ballroom.

415
00:30:50,334 --> 00:30:54,838
If she sees either of us and can't find Batista, it's going to be bad.

416
00:30:58,425 --> 00:30:59,677
Here, take this.

417
00:31:00,427 --> 00:31:03,180
Take the elevator down, go through the garage.

418
00:31:03,514 --> 00:31:04,431
How will you get out?

419
00:31:04,682 --> 00:31:05,683
I'll hitchhike.

420
00:31:06,600 --> 00:31:07,393
Okay.

421
00:31:23,117 --> 00:31:24,076
No.

422
00:31:24,368 --> 00:31:25,244
No!

423
00:31:30,166 --> 00:31:32,043
Help, over here!

424
00:31:34,086 --> 00:31:36,422
What's the matter? You like it here.

425
00:31:37,423 --> 00:31:40,134
Please, don't kill me. I'm begging you.

426
00:31:40,593 --> 00:31:41,844
Oh god, oh god!

427
00:31:42,345 --> 00:31:44,514
Quiet, don't be so scared.

428
00:31:47,350 --> 00:31:51,521
You said it yourself, death is a natural, necessary part of life.

429
00:31:52,271 --> 00:31:54,232
I'll give you anything you want.

430
00:31:54,774 --> 00:31:56,609
You'll be living in luxury.

431
00:31:57,276 --> 00:31:58,111
I'll pass.

432
00:31:59,654 --> 00:32:00,697
What about your son?

433
00:32:01,239 --> 00:32:04,284
Don't you want Harrison to get into a good college?

434
00:32:05,076 --> 00:32:07,704
I'll give you so much money, your grandchildren will have enough.

435
00:32:08,246 --> 00:32:09,706
Don't you dare say my son's name.

436
00:32:10,248 --> 00:32:12,459
Okay, okay. God!

437
00:32:15,587 --> 00:32:18,590
None of this would have happened if you had just killed that cop.

438
00:32:19,257 --> 00:32:21,718
Sorry to disappoint, but I don't kill good people.

439
00:32:22,218 --> 00:32:23,678
A serial killer has a conscience?

440
00:32:23,929 --> 00:32:25,221
A code.

441
00:32:26,139 --> 00:32:28,016
Given to me by my father.

442
00:32:31,436 --> 00:32:34,564
He understood that my childhood predetermined my destiny.

443
00:32:35,232 --> 00:32:38,401
Just as your childhood made you who you are.

444
00:32:42,113 --> 00:32:44,407
But my father was a man of justice.

445
00:32:46,076 --> 00:32:47,786
He taught me to kill bad people.

446
00:32:48,536 --> 00:32:52,624
That's why I was intrigued when I found Red's invitation to your dinner.

447
00:32:54,251 --> 00:32:56,586
A buffet of killers for every taste.

448
00:32:57,170 --> 00:32:57,963
To feed my urges.

449
00:32:59,631 --> 00:33:01,425
But then I came here.

450
00:33:03,510 --> 00:33:05,554
I was surrounded by like-minded people.

451
00:33:07,139 --> 00:33:08,348
It was an intoxicating feeling.

452
00:33:08,682 --> 00:33:10,267
This is what I've always dreamed of.

453
00:33:10,517 --> 00:33:11,185
I know.

454
00:33:11,518 --> 00:33:14,271
A place for people like you, where they can be themselves.

455
00:33:14,772 --> 00:33:16,523
We all want to be real.

456
00:33:16,773 --> 00:33:25,783
Yes, I listened to Ella, and Lula, and Mia, and Gareth. They boasted so freely, openly, and with such feeling about their kills.

457
00:33:30,704 --> 00:33:32,414
It was quite a revelation.

458
00:33:32,706 --> 00:33:34,708
I knew you'd like it. I knew it.

459
00:33:35,417 --> 00:33:44,718
But then I realized that all their victims were innocent people. And we weren't so like-minded after all.

460
00:33:46,554 --> 00:33:48,013
Sports betting!

461
00:33:48,472 --> 00:33:49,431
1xBet!

462
00:33:50,099 --> 00:33:51,225
The moment is coming!

463
00:33:51,767 --> 00:33:52,726
1xBet!

464
00:33:53,394 --> 00:33:54,770
Team, forward!

465
00:33:55,730 --> 00:33:56,689
1xBet!

466
00:33:57,398 --> 00:33:59,025
Victory will come!

467
00:33:59,442 --> 00:34:01,777
Stay with the one who believes in your success.

468
00:34:04,113 --> 00:34:05,823
Your team, your success.

469
00:34:13,372 --> 00:34:15,708
1xBet - this is your victory.

470
00:34:32,266 --> 00:34:34,060
Your offer is tempting.

471
00:34:35,228 --> 00:34:39,107
A chance to give my son wealth instead of the trauma of several generations.

472
00:34:40,525 --> 00:34:44,112
But here I realized something about myself.

473
00:34:46,239 --> 00:34:50,118
Perhaps the pursuit of justice runs in our family.

474
00:34:52,578 --> 00:34:55,248
So it's not about the thrill of the kill itself?

475
00:34:57,417 --> 00:34:59,127
That's right, both.

476
00:35:01,629 --> 00:35:05,425
Excellent. Smile wider, this concerns everyone.

477
00:35:06,134 --> 00:35:07,468
She's talking about you, chin up.

478
00:35:07,760 --> 00:35:10,346
I prefer not to smile without a good reason.

479
00:35:10,513 --> 00:35:10,972
I know.

480
00:35:11,264 --> 00:35:12,682
How much longer do I have to be here?

481
00:35:13,182 --> 00:35:14,267
We have to wait for Prater.

482
00:35:14,517 --> 00:35:15,643
He'll be here soon.

483
00:35:16,144 --> 00:35:17,687
Where is he? I don't see him.

484
00:35:18,229 --> 00:35:21,733
Mayor Thompson, do us the honor of announcing the results of the fundraiser.

485
00:35:22,191 --> 00:35:23,234
I thought Leon would do it.

486
00:35:23,568 --> 00:35:24,694
Is he still not here?

487
00:35:25,194 --> 00:35:26,112
I'm going home.

488
00:35:26,487 --> 00:35:29,615
Please stay on stage. There will be an important announcement soon.

489
00:35:32,410 --> 00:35:33,703
Good evening, everyone.

490
00:35:34,203 --> 00:35:36,122
Please, look at the clock.

491
00:35:36,539 --> 00:35:39,333
It's almost time to announce the results.

492
00:35:40,293 --> 00:35:45,465
So, 5, 4, 3, 2, 1!

493
00:35:48,342 --> 00:35:54,724
If we add Leon Prater's generous donation, we have raised $22.8 million.

494
00:35:58,269 --> 00:35:59,312
Leon, where are you?

495
00:35:59,854 --> 00:36:04,442
Leon! Leon! Leon! Leon!

496
00:36:15,745 --> 00:36:17,372
Quiet, you're just...

497
00:36:17,580 --> 00:36:19,290
Leon! Leon!

498
00:36:20,333 --> 00:36:22,252
Enjoy it while you can.

499
00:36:23,211 --> 00:36:28,842
Because when you disappear, you'll be remembered as a cop killer with evidence on serial killers.

500
00:36:30,302 --> 00:36:31,136
No!

501
00:36:41,438 --> 00:36:42,856
I won't be your trophy.

502
00:36:43,481 --> 00:36:45,358
No, you won't.

503
00:36:46,234 --> 00:36:47,235
Oh, god.

504
00:36:47,569 --> 00:36:48,445
My god.

505
00:36:50,447 --> 00:36:52,699
I knew I could convince you.

506
00:36:54,201 --> 00:36:56,828
No one turns down that kind of money. No one.

507
00:36:57,788 --> 00:36:58,580
Wow.

508
00:36:59,122 --> 00:36:59,706
No.

509
00:37:02,125 --> 00:37:03,460
I'm going to kill you anyway.

510
00:37:03,710 --> 00:37:04,586
But you said...

511
00:37:04,836 --> 00:37:06,630
I keep trophies as mementos.

512
00:37:08,256 --> 00:37:10,217
And I don't want to remember you.

513
00:38:14,357 --> 00:38:17,819
That's it, I'm definitely going home. I value my time and I want to get some sleep.

514
00:38:18,361 --> 00:38:19,362
I'll walk you out.

515
00:38:19,654 --> 00:38:22,657
No need, I'll get there myself. Thanks.

516
00:38:27,537 --> 00:38:28,496
What's the matter?

517
00:38:45,513 --> 00:38:48,933
Are you going to join in, or are you just going to stand there and watch?

518
00:39:23,101 --> 00:39:23,726
Goodbye.

519
00:39:25,728 --> 00:39:27,564
This time for good.

520
00:39:36,364 --> 00:39:39,492
It seems this private yacht is looking for a new owner.

521
00:39:47,375 --> 00:39:50,336
It's time to show the world the real Leon Prater.

522
00:40:02,515 --> 00:40:04,517
That's the penthouse alarm.

523
00:40:05,018 --> 00:40:05,977
Davis, with me!

524
00:40:29,126 --> 00:40:29,668
In here!

525
00:40:31,378 --> 00:40:32,671
Search everything here.

526
00:40:33,172 --> 00:40:34,548
Tony, turn off the alarm.

527
00:40:35,466 --> 00:40:36,300
In there.

528
00:40:41,263 --> 00:40:42,890
What the hell is this place?

529
00:40:46,268 --> 00:40:47,103
We need to report this.

530
00:40:47,436 --> 00:40:49,522
There's no one to report to, we're all here.

531
00:40:51,524 --> 00:40:52,650
We have a body here.

532
00:40:53,609 --> 00:40:55,277
And a gun.

533
00:41:03,452 --> 00:41:04,578
Oh my God!

534
00:41:08,207 --> 00:41:11,168
Returning to the water is a kind of resurrection.

535
00:41:11,794 --> 00:41:13,671
But this time it's different.

536
00:41:14,213 --> 00:41:16,382
Harry gave me the code so I wouldn't get caught.

537
00:41:16,799 --> 00:41:19,260
So I could control my urges.

538
00:41:25,266 --> 00:41:26,267
Is Prater still not here?

539
00:41:26,517 --> 00:41:26,976
No.

540
00:41:27,351 --> 00:41:29,603
Well, guess whose prints are on the gun.

541
00:41:30,521 --> 00:41:31,480
Wait.

542
00:41:33,607 --> 00:41:35,776
This belonged to Captain Batista.

543
00:41:48,372 --> 00:41:49,331
Claudette.

544
00:41:50,332 --> 00:41:51,333
Come here.

545
00:41:58,424 --> 00:41:59,425
Take a look.

546
00:42:08,349 --> 00:42:10,518
Don Framp, the New York Ripper.

547
00:42:11,435 --> 00:42:13,229
But my urges are changing.

548
00:42:18,609 --> 00:42:23,030
When I rose from the dead, I thought I was doomed to a lonely existence.

549
00:42:23,614 --> 00:42:24,782
What's happening?

550
00:42:25,283 --> 00:42:27,118
We're leaving this cesspool.

551
00:42:27,618 --> 00:42:29,203
What? Where are we going?

552
00:42:29,704 --> 00:42:31,539
Home. Home?

553
00:42:32,206 --> 00:42:33,916
We're going back to Amherst.

554
00:42:35,126 --> 00:42:37,420
I bought the house you raised me in.

555
00:42:37,670 --> 00:42:40,465
What about your job? Your students?

556
00:42:41,299 --> 00:42:43,467
We have a lot to talk about.

557
00:42:51,267 --> 00:42:53,603
But maybe I'm not meant to be alone.

558
00:42:56,314 --> 00:42:59,609
I need people like Blessing and his family.

559
00:43:00,109 --> 00:43:03,154
As Al said, even people like me need company.

560
00:43:04,322 --> 00:43:06,491
Harry taught me to lean on Deb.

561
00:43:07,575 --> 00:43:08,910
But she's gone now.

562
00:43:10,328 --> 00:43:11,537
I miss her.

563
00:43:12,413 --> 00:43:14,249
But I have Harrison.

564
00:43:15,250 --> 00:43:16,584
I'm his support.

565
00:43:17,418 --> 00:43:22,465
And when my dark urges flare up, I can rely on him.

566
00:43:23,633 --> 00:43:26,135
And so I will become more human.

567
00:43:27,262 --> 00:43:28,638
More grounded.

568
00:43:32,475 --> 00:43:35,520
I will always remember why I do what I do.

569
00:43:59,461 --> 00:44:01,296
I used to dream of being different.

570
00:44:02,547 --> 00:44:03,673
Normal.

571
00:44:05,342 --> 00:44:07,469
To live without the Dark Passenger.

572
00:44:10,639 --> 00:44:12,224
But who am I kidding?

573
00:44:14,351 --> 00:44:15,685
This is the real me.

574
00:44:16,478 --> 00:44:18,146
This is my nature.

575
00:44:19,272 --> 00:44:20,607
I am Dexter Morgan.

576
00:44:21,191 --> 00:44:23,318
And I am who I'm supposed to be.

577
00:44:24,277 --> 00:44:27,280
And who you want me to be.